# Minimum Codex CLI version harness v1 is tested against.
# Format: semver string on first non-comment line.
# Setup skill compares `codex --version` output to this pin and refuses
# registration with a structured error (see doc/harness/codex-troubleshooting.md
# "Codex 1.x.y required, found 1.a.b") when the installed CLI is older.
#
# Why the pin: Codex tool naming has churned in pre-1.0 (issue #2235
# apply_patch vs shell). Bounding the test matrix to a known-good version
# prevents silent semantic drift between this codebase's assumptions and
# the user's CLI. Bump the pin only after the AC-002 apply_patch matrix
# and AC-001 hook payload schema have been re-validated against the new
# Codex version.
#
# Bump procedure (codified for future maintainers):
#   1. Update this file to the new minimum version.
#   2. Re-run AC-001 + AC-002 verification against the new Codex.
#   3. Update doc/harness/codex-payload-deltas.md if schemas changed.
#   4. Note the bump in CHANGELOG.md.

